{
  "title": "RGB content overlap between the archived seven-scene comparison and M-SWIR-RGB",
  "sample": "Ten archived test patches were examined for each of groups 1 to 7, each against the corresponding RGB mosaic C1 to C7. The check covers these 70 selected views. Other archived patches, C8 to C10 and alternative patch/site pairs were not tested.",
  "matching": "SIFT ratio test (0.70) on patch vs. RGB mosaic at 0.25x and 0.5x scale, followed by a RANSAC homography. For each scale, feature locations on the patch were deduplicated and split into 70% fit / 30% held out; the holdout reprojection error is measured on the 256-pixel patch grid. The final stored H refits all matches and maps the patch grid into the full mosaic grid. Acceptance requires at least 12 inliers, at least 0.12 patch-area coverage and at least four held-out matches at <3 px comprising at least half the holdout, with median error among those matches <1.5 px; the linear scale must fall between 0.4 and 20.",
  "result": "67 of 70 selected RGB patches matched, with at least one correspondence in each of C1 to C7. Three inconclusive C4 patches are included. Matches establish overlapping scene content; the archived crops do not identify the constituent original exposures.",
  "bench_sample_link": {
    "file": "data_quality_windows.csv",
    "file_sha256_lf": "1c133e3091c74c7849d5947fdb96a321c9172dd31d81323ebcae7df462fc80d8",
    "set": "chen",
    "split": "test",
    "quality_fields": [
      "a_lag1",
      "b_lag1",
      "a_psd",
      "b_psd",
      "ab_r0",
      "ab_peak",
      "ab_shift"
    ],
    "procedure": "For each of the 67 matched patches the retained SWIR and RGB PNG hashes were verified against the matching record. Applying evidence_code/data_quality_stats.py to each pair reproduces the seven archived window statistics to their published precision. The full tuple identifies exactly one row among 3715 archived patches, with the expected filename and split. The benchmark table contains statistics rather than per-image byte hashes. For the three inconclusive patches only filename and split were checked against the benchmark table."
  },
  "swir_channel_identity": {
    "meaning": "B1/B2/B4 are nominal archive channel labels in decoded PNG order. This is an archive-content assignment; the mapping of each original exposure to a physical filter was not verified across data versions.",
    "channel_1": "35 PNGs were compared with independent B1 single-band image representations.",
    "channel_2": "35 PNGs were compared with the corresponding channels of the B123, B125, B234 and B245 combinations.",
    "channel_3": "All 3715 B124 PNGs have channel 3 exactly equal to the independent single-band B4 PNG (pixel comparison). The SWIR PNG SHA-256 in all 70 sample rows also matches the input hash in that comparison."
  },
